[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_item")
id = "book_riverwatch_roll"
display_name = "The Riverwatch Roll"
description = "A roll of names on oiled hide, left in a niche at the mouth of the old barrow."
value = 5
weight = 0.5
book_text = "THE ROLL OF THE RIVERWATCH COMPANY
set down in the third year of the Pact

These are the men who held the ford for the Pact, and put out the lights of the Greywater, and were paid in land for it.

Osric Vane, of Hallam's own company. Forty lights, put out with his own hook. Captain, and given the ford.
Aldo Brannoch, his sergeant. Twenty-two lights. Given the north field.
Berit the Tall. Nineteen lights. Given the mill.
Hamund Grey. Eleven lights, and two that would not go out, which he caged and sold to the Collegium at Ilunhall for a great price.

Let it be remembered that the lights asked for mercy in their own tongue, and that we were told this tongue was a trick, and that we believed it.

Let it be remembered that we built the garrison on the place where we burned the last of them, so that nobody would dig there.

The Pact pays well. Ilun keep us."
